253 - There's No Other Name Like Jesus
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 253
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[F]There's no other name like Jesus, 'Tis [C]the dearest [C7]name we know,
[C7/E]'Tis the angel's [F]joy in heaven, 'Tis the Christian's joy below.
[F]Sweet name, dear name, [C]There's no [C7]other name like Jesus;
[F]Sweet name, dear name, There's no other name like Jesus.

Refrain:
[C]Sweet name, (sweet name) [C7]dear name, (dear name)
[C7]There's [F]no other name like Jesus;
[F]Sweet name, (sweet name) dear name, (dear name)
[C]There's no [C7]other name like Jesus.

Verse 2:
[F]There's no other name [C]like [C7]Jesus
[C7/E]When [F]the heart with grief is sad,
[F]There's no [C]other [C7]name like Jesus
[F]When the heart is free and glad.

Verse 3:
[F]'Tis the hope that I [C]shall see [C7]Him
[C7/E]When [F]in glory He appears,
[F]'Tis the hope [C]to [C7]hear His welcome
[F]That my fainting spirit cheers.

Verse 4:
[F]If He wills that I [C]should labor
[C7/E]In [F]His vineyard day by day,
[F]Then 'tis well [C]if [C7]only Jesus
[F]Blesses all I do or say.

Verse 5:
[F]If He wills that death's [C]cold finger
[C7/E]Touch [F]my feeble, mortal clay,
[F]Then 'tis well [C]if [C7]only Jesus
[F]Is my dying trust and stay.
